# Line endings are normalised, because a commit made on Windows otherwise
# rewrites whole files invisibly.
#
# This is not hypothetical here. `8c47ac4` landed from the Windows peer in
# CRLF and changed 118 lines of `link.rs` and `cursio.rs` — but git saw every
# one of their 1743 lines as modified, so merging the Apple branch reported
# both files as conflicting in their entirety. The real overlap only became
# visible with `-X ignore-cr-at-eol`. Text is stored LF and checked out LF on
# every platform; the Rust, C and MSVC toolchains all read it either way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files Windows tooling insists on writing back as CRLF. Left alone rather
# than fought with: normalising them means every save by Visual Studio shows
# up as a diff.
*.sln text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj.filters text eol=crlf
*.inf text eol=crlf
*.rc text eol=crlf

# Binary, so never touched: normalisation would corrupt them silently.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
